  "findings": [
    "All 336 main four-host fault cases and 120 EINTR supplement cases match the current policy; local development checks add 84 and 30 cases. No new production read-policy defect is reproduced.",
    "Forty injected EINTR responses produce 41 libc opens before success. Forty EINTR plus four ENOENT produce 45. The finite Rust-call bound must not be described as a libc/syscall/RPC count bound.",
    "All 1200 post-publication natural raw-file opens succeed on the first attempt after prior NotFound priming. The 4 MiB group nevertheless contains a 71.509 ms open sample."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "NameBy is a conditional attempt bound within each data attempt; natural observations do not establish it for future executions. VisibleBy is also attempt-based, never a millisecond bound.",
    "ReadLookup abstracts complete data authentication into one action and starts after namespace resolution; ReadAttempt separately models descriptor/index/envelope/payload ordering. Neither proves full adapter conformance or a composed refinement.",
    "Fault injection modifies only selected libc open return values and returned payload buffers. It does not change on-disk data or sleep behavior, send real signals, cover arbitrary syscall families/threads, or establish a natural failure rate.",
    "The original and EINTR probes have separately archived source/shim hashes. Earlier runs are not relabeled with the later probe version.",
    "Natural tests use raw files and three peer readers per writer with SSH control. Open latency begins at the reader call; read verification includes open/read/hash. Reply timing includes coordinator collection. No cross-machine clock subtraction, cache eviction or system-wide load isolation. Some proof checks overlap measurements.",
    "Raw fixtures are removed after all reader workers exit and are not counted as straw GC. straw fault fixtures are reclaimed through normal GC, then their private metadata and remote programs are removed.",
    "Production sources and 21 Verus inputs are unchanged. Positive Verus verification is fresh; 105 semantic negative controls and 782 Python/40 native tests are reused only after exact source checks.",
    "No new 100 GB/physical TB workload, full Rust I/O proof, unbounded interruption progress proof, hard deadline, bandwidth SLA or full-system bug-free claim."
  ],
